Subject: Frameless call classifiers

What this does
  Frameless call classifiers.

Why we need it
  The `call`/`call_method` threaded classifiers inlined the lazy-materialize call, so the compiler kept a stack frame across it and every dispatch of a JS call paid the prologue even though no eligible call reaches it.

What it adds
  The lazy branch moves to separate noinline `regvm_t_call_lazy`/`regvm_t_call_method_lazy`; the classifier is a tag test, a class-id test, a ready-byte test and a jump; the gate's handler frame check now also fails on any push/pop in those two handlers, which the `[sp]`-based check could not see on x86.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
